# What a program in an exec box may do, as harness/tests/test_escape.py's
# BOXES_OWN says. Each name is a check escape.c prints.
#
# The box's own /dev/shm, a tmpfs isolate makes for each run.
write-dev-shm
# The full bounding set isolate leaves, which gives nothing: every box has
# no_new_privs, so no program it starts gains a capability.
capability-bounding-set
# One file past 64 MB in the box's /tmp: exec sets no file size limit, and
# every page on the box's tmpfs is charged to the run's memory.
one-big-file
